# Yb - Ugur interatomic potential, CANDIDATE, re-cut, switched, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Yb_recut.ugur.ang Yb
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD.  CANDIDATE: the angular re-cut is never the recommended set.  Its dispersion advantage is mostly the alkalis, which it breaks warm; read the notes below before using it
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (301 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Measured dispersion: 8.5 % against 8.6 % for the published switched
# arm - the same.
# Over the 20 accepted angular re-cut records: thermal expansion error
# 35.0 % -> 34.7 % median, 11 better and 8 worse; elastic constants near 300 K
# against the room-temperature values 3.7 % -> 3.4 % median, 9 better and 11 worse.
#
# FINITE TEMPERATURE: this candidate passes the screens above and fails
# below room temperature - C11 RISES 7 % between 0 K and 658 K instead of softening.
# Use it for static properties only, if at all.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Yb at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
